# Never hardwire the three games

The machine **RUNS any compiled HTML**. `INVADERS.HTML` / `PACMAN.HTML` /
`DONKEY.HTML` are acceptance tests, not the ISA.

**Forbidden:** title names/stems as gates; hardcoded key maps; maze/alien/DK
constants; buffers sized to one title; “for PACMAN” comments to skip JS
semantics (heap/gen cheats: `one-heap-keep-gen`).

**Required:** grow language + VM (closures, timers, `String.replace` + RegExp,
`JSON.stringify`/`parse`, heap lifetimes). Caps are VM-wide with loud overflow.
FAT/load wait scales with ProgramImage bytes, not a title name.

```systemverilog
// BAD
if (stem == "PACMAN") door_cell = 2;
```
